! mcp_bootstrap_p247.strap -- MCP printed page 247: the tape-read retry
! tail of the UK error-recovery package (CBZ,$15,RYNOGD .. RDNOTP and
! the BZB,2.12($13),RCENT1 that leaves the page), lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.254, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CB000206  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 247" (prefix glyph
! round; the right-hand serials print 0B/DB, see below); the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 227765, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, all located, contiguous from 227765.00 to
! 230020.40 (line 50 is a full-word BZB, so the next location is
! 230021.40).  No remarks.  The volume OCR puts p.246's last row,
! "RUK LC,$15,RTTRY", at 227764.40, so line 1 joins it.  Asterisks
! after the LOCATION on lines 7, 9, 30.
!   lines 1-8    the retry count / branch to RYBSP; BE,VRT twice
!   line  9      RDREXT DRZ(BU,32),4 -- prints 000002.00 (two words);
!                a reservation, so no !CHECK (transcription_workflow
!                3a); its extent is pinned by line 10's 227773.00
!   lines 10-17  four LV,VU,RDREXT-.32 / B,$ pairs (stop loops)
!   lines 18-20  RTTRY, RTSP3X, RBSP3X: CF count fields, print 000004,
!                000004, 000005 (C22-6728's "Retry Count Fields")
!   lines 21-50  RUKSRT .. RDNOTP
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * "RCREXT" on lines 21 and 23 is RDREXT: BZB prints 227772.11 and
!     227772.14 = RDREXT (227771.00) + 1.09 / + 1.12.  At 900 dpi the
!     second glyph of lines 4, 21, 23 has a straight left stem (D).
!   * line 42 "LVI,$15,RCREXT" is a DIFFERENT symbol, RCREXT: it prints
!     230175.37, not RDREXT's 227771; the glyph is round with no stem,
!     and C22-6728 names both RCREXT and RDREXT.
!   * line 30 prints "REJJCB.62"; written REJJOB.  C22-6728 prints
!     REJJOB 28 times (REJJCB once), "REJJOB.62 on, a UK total failure
!     has occurred"; this drum prints O open.  Nothing landed spells it.
!   * line 40's label prints RDNCTP; written RDNOTP: C22-6728's typeset
!     prose prints RDNOTP ("jam, which is taken care of by RDNOTP"),
!     and p.246 line 41's BXE reference reads with O.  This drum prints
!     O open, so the open glyph here does not argue for C.
!   * line 40's label RDNOTP: second glyph has a straight stem (D) at
!     900 dpi; nothing references it on this page -- rests on ink.
!   * line 1 RYNOGD: written with the letter O (R Y NO GooD); round
!     glyph; nothing landed spells it.  Volume OCR reads "RYNCGC".
!   * octal fields "CCCCCC.CC" etc. are 0; line 34's "CCCCCC.CC 8F".
!   * line 41's byte prints "BO"/"8O"; written B0 (see !CHECK).
!   * line 47 "VF,CCCW" is VF,DCCW (D worn): prints 000002.00+ = DCCW.
!   * "DMCP" on lines 31, 46 is the D-name as printed (DMCP SYN 32.0).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials 0B000206 .. 0B000236 (prefix glyph
! round, header prints CB000206).  Shared serials: lines 3/4 (208),
! 6/7/8 (210), 10/11 (212), 12/13 (213), 14/15 (214), 16/17 (215),
! 26/27 (224), 31-34 (228), 35/36 (229), 37/38 (230), 40/41 (232),
! 42/43 (233), 44/45 (234), 46-49 (235).  No serial is skipped.

